<BehaviorPatch #track.r_2_0_2_6_-_0_8_-_0_3_-_0_3_1_7_-_a_d_d_-_i_n_d_e_x_e_d_d_b_-_r_e_v_i_s_i_o_n_e_d_-_v_f_s_-_a_u_t_h_o_r_i_t_y.behavior_patch.xnl-revisioned-persistence apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" version="1" { capability = "xnl-revisioned-persistence" } (
  <Mutations [
    <Upsert { selector = "behavior://xnl-revisioned-persistence/requirements/browser-persistent-authority" } (
      <Requirement #browser-persistent-authority (
        <Statement ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WAD9>
        An IndexedDB revisioned VFS authority SHALL durably retain one authority-qualified snapshot and live revision, and SHALL linearize freshness validation, semantic no-op detection, and accepted snapshot/revision replacement in one browser-storage transaction.
        </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WAD9>
        <Suites [
          <Suite #indexeddb-authority { name = "IndexedDB revisioned authority" } (
            <Cases [
              <Case #reopen-retains-fact (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADA>
                An authority has accepted and durably stored a snapshot revision.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADA>
                <When ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADB>
                A new authority instance opens the same database and authority identity.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADB>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADC>
                It SHALL restore the exact snapshot and revision and SHALL NOT overwrite them with its initial seed.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADC>
              )>
              <Case #independent-instance-cas (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADD>
                Two independently opened authority instances submit different candidates from the same current revision.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADD>
                <When ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADE>
                IndexedDB linearizes their readwrite transactions.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADE>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADF>
                Exactly one SHALL return applied with workspace durability, the other SHALL return conflict, and reopen SHALL expose the winning snapshot and revision.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADF>
              )>
              <Case #browser-failure-is-atomic (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADG>
                An IndexedDB transaction aborts or fails before durable completion.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADG>
                <When ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADH>
                The authority returns a failed result and is reopened.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADH>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADJ>
                The previous snapshot and revision SHALL remain authoritative and a retry from that revision MAY succeed.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADJ>
              )>
              <Case #browser-safe-public-surface (
                <Given ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADK>
                A browser consumer imports the explicit xnl-vfs/revisioned-persistence subpath.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADK>
                <When ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADM>
                It creates the IndexedDB authority through the public factory.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADM>
                <Then ?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADN>
                The subpath's reachable implementation SHALL use no Node-only builtins and SHALL preserve the existing RevisionedVfsAuthority and VCS-separation contracts without making a new browser-safety claim for the package root.
                </?01M1W1C2DJPW5927QANX76WADN>
              )>
            ]>
          )>
        ]>
      )>
    )>
  ]>
)>
